From b22bd7272def070b9a0e69d0f42fb3e86e1076af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Manrique <125496885+hashd1ve@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 23:26:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 27/29] dsv41: a marked prompt pass's edits, lens, mixes and
 streams (xedit.zig)

TF_DS_XEDIT=MiB on every rank (unset: no buffer, no launch, no frame). A request with "edits": "name" has its prompt
pass change the streams entering the listed layers as DIR/name.xedit says (add, patch, ablate, set, on the streams of
a mask), on both ranks alike: rank 0 sends the plan and its rows (fill_mark, fill_xdata) before the first chunk. With
"taps": "lens": 1|2 writes the head's logits of the last position at each tapped layer (the layer's own pre, then
each stream alone); "streams": K the streams themselves of the last K positions; and every marked pass's file now
holds the prompt's logits and every sublayer's pre, post and comb. TF_DS_XTAPS_ROWS bounds a marked pass's chunk.
A planned pass runs whole from the prompt's first token, apart from the prompt cache, and nothing cuts into it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
